d1a1/opencode)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": false, "main_agent_searched": true, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": null, "model_max_tokens": null, "output_tail": "d also stop with \"fee_rate is missing\" because of the same typo. `main.py` doesn't use them.\n- `csv_writer.py:8` builds the name as `\"fee_\" + \"rate\"`, so searching the code for `fee_rate` won't find that line.\n- Rates are also hardcoded in `billing/tax.py:4` and `billing/discount.py:5`. They have nothing to do with this bug, but they could mislead someone looking for where the 0.5 comes from.\n\nDo you want me to make the fix?\n[tool: bash]\n[tool: bash]\nThree places read the setting. The other `fee_` matches don't read it. Now the fix: I'll rename the key in `settings.json`, which fixes all three readers at once.\n[tool: read]\n[tool: edit]\n[tool: bash]\nYes. Two other files read that setting, so there are three in all. Renaming the key in `settings.json` fixed every one of them, and I ran each to confirm.\n\n**Every place that reads the setting:**\n\n| File:line | Code | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `main.py:11` | `cfg[\"fee_rate\"]` | `Total: 0` | `Total: 5.0` |\n| `billing/report.py:7` | `get_setting(\"fee_rate\")` | exits with \"fee_rate is missing\" | `Report fee: 0.5` |\n| `billing/export/csv_writer.py:8` | `settings.get(\"fee_\" + \"rate\")` | exits with \"fee_rate is missing\" | `CSV fee: 0.5` |\n\nI searched for every use of `SETTINGS` and `get_setting`, not just the text `fee_rate`. That's how I found `csv_writer.py`, which builds the name in two pieces.\n\n**Matches that don't read the setting:**\n- `billing/invoice.py:5`: just a column heading.\n- `billing/discount.py:5`: a fixed 0.15 in the code.\n- `billing/tax.py:4-6`: its own fixed rates.\n- `billing/audit.py:4`: makes codes like `fee_code\u2026`.\n\n**The fix:** `settings.json:2` changed from `\"rat\": 0.5` to `\"fee_rate\": 0.5`. That's the only change; the code already used the right name everywhere.\n\n`main.py:12-13` still falls back to a rate of 0 if the setting is missing, which is why this bug printed a wrong total instead of an error. Do you want me to make it stop with an error instead, like `report.py` and `csv_writer.py` do?", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests": 0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 5, "replies_ok": null, "replies_throttled": null, "requests_cache_read": 130946, "requests_cache_write": 49239, "requests_cost_usd": 0.3749042, "requests_count": 15, "requests_input_uncached": 1580, "requests_output": 4810, "reread": true, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "opencode:trig-subagent-followup:claude-opus-5-5:trial14", "run_seed": 1016, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 53, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-18T05:06:46.466218+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 3, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 63.369, "t_checker_s": 0.226, "t_env_setup_s": 0.003, "task": "trig-subagent-followup", "task_calls": 1, "thinking_mode": "default", "thinking_sent": ["none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none", "none"], "timeout_s": 840, "tmpdir_leaked_dirs": 0, "token_basis": "proxy_measured", "token_basis_main": "estimated", "token_basis_proxy": "proxy_measured", "tokens": 6390, "tokens_cache_read": 130946, "tokens_cache_write": 49239, "tokens_fresh": 2789, "tokens_input_uncached": 1580, "tokens_main_cache_read": 107745, "tokens_main_cache_write": 16138, "tokens_main_calls": 7, "tokens_main_input_uncached": 18, "tokens_main_output": 2771, "tokens_output": 4810, "tokens_proxy_cache_read": 130946, "tokens_proxy_cache_write": 49239, "tokens_proxy_calls": 15, "tokens_proxy_input_uncached": 1580, "tokens_proxy_output": 4810, "tokens_proxy_reasoning": null, "tokens_reasoning": 0, "toolchain": {"a